            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000:F006\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposed edit provides an independently usable and complete summary of the covered entity's permission to require an entrance medical examination and condition an offer on its results. It accurately captures all three conjunctive statutory conditions under (A), (B), and (C), and fully spells out the three confidentiality exceptions in (B)(i)-(iii), including the specific scopes and threshold conditions for disclosures to supervisors/managers and first aid/safety personnel.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F000\", \"F001\", \"F002\", \"F006\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The edit misrepresents the statutory requirements by stating that the permission applies if 'any one of these three alternative conditions is met'. In the source text, paragraphs (A), (B), and (C) are cumulative conjunctive requirements linked by 'and', not disjunctive alternatives.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0002\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F002\", \"F003\", \"F004\", \"F005\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The unchanged draft reading is incomplete for independent use because it abbreviates the confidentiality exceptions into a high-level parenthetical, omitting the specific substantive boundaries and conditions governing disclosure to supervisors and managers (necessary restrictions and accommodations) and first aid/safety personnel (when appropriate, if emergency treatment might be required).\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
